 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Solía: used to",
    "@en": "Used to: used to"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Used to** + verbo = solía, antes hacía. **I used to play football** = solía jugar al fútbol (ahora ya no).",
     "@en": "**Used to** + verb = used, before. **I used to play football** = used to play football (now not anymore)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Se pronuncia «yúst-tu». Solo sirve para el pasado y para cosas que ya no pasan.",
     "@en": "It's pronounced «yúst-tu». It only serves the past and things that don't happen anymore."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Negar y preguntar",
    "@en": "Deny and ask"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "Negativa: **didn't use to** (no solía). Pregunta: **Did you use to…?** (¿solías…?).",
     "@en": "Negative: **didn't use to** (not used to). Question: **Did you use to…?** (used to?)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Ojo: en la negación no lleva -d: **I didn't use to**, no «didn't used to».",
     "@en": "Eye: in denial does not carry -d: **I didn't use to**, not «didn't used to»."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Cuidado con «be used to»",
    "@en": "Watch out for «be used to»"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**Be used to** + -ing significa «estar acostumbrado a». No es lo mismo que **used to**, aunque se parezca.",
     "@en": "**Be used to** + -ing means «to be used to». It's not the same as **used to**, even if it looks like it."
    }
   ]
  },
